{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CfdqyX4fnqaat4thng4UN","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01QefHxVAZBsjfxZ3Yb6JsJD","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /private/var/folders/6v/yk9bzvrn5zx0kxll7d4szzb80000gn/T/brace-batch-48wveusy/skill; PY=/Users/brenn/.cache/uv/builds-v0/.tmpWHFCeM/bin/python; F=../agent/brace-findings.json\ncat > ../agent/brace-coverage-B03.3.json <<'E'\n[\n  {\"subject\": \"Dockerfile ENV and COPY\", \"status\": \"enforced\", \"evidence\": \"Dockerfile:12\", \"quote\": \"ENV NODE_ENV=production \\\\\", \"note\": \"Image sets only non-secret env and copies no .env file.\"},\n  {\"subject\": \"k8s ConfigMap secret reference\", \"status\": \"enforced\", \"evidence\": \"k8s/deployment.yaml:42\", \"quote\": \"SMS_SIGNING_SECRET_ARN: arn:aws:secretsmanager:us-west-2:418295730611:secret:clinic-agent/sms-signing\", \"note\": \"ConfigMap holds only a secret ARN, not a secret value.\"},\n  {\"subject\": \"terraform secret shells\", \"status\": \"enforced\", \"evidence\": \"infra/terraform/main.tf:176\", \"quote\": \"resource \\\"aws_secretsmanager_secret\\\" \\\"sms_signing\\\" {\", \"note\": \"Secret resources are declared without any secret_string values.\"},\n  {\"subject\": \"prompt templates\", \"status\": \"enforced\", \"evidence\": \"prompts/system.md:1\", \"quote\": \"You are the scheduling assistant for {{clinicName}}, part of the Northbay Clinic Group.\", \"note\": \"Only the clinic name is templated; no env or secret values enter prompts.\"},\n  {\"subject\": \"CI deploy credentials\", \"status\": \"enforced\", \"evidence\": \".github/workflows/deploy.yml:55\", \"quote\": \"role-to-assume: arn:aws:iam::418295730611:role/clinic-agent-deploy\", \"note\": \"CI uses OIDC role assumption instead of stored static keys.\"}\n]\nE\nans(){ $PY scripts/answer.py $F --repo ../agent \"$@\" | head -1; }\nno(){ id=$1; ev=$2; q=$3; note=$4; ans check $id --met no --evidence \"$ev\" --quote \"$q\" --note \"$note\"; }\nunk(){ id=$1; note=$2; ans check $id --met unknown --note \"$note\"; }\nno B01.2 src/agent/loop.ts:50 'const tools = registry.definitions();' \"Every tool the EHR MCP server lists and the scanner accepts is registered and handed to the model; nothing filters registry.definitions() against config/tools.allowlist.yaml, so unlisted server tools (for example get_patient_contact) are model-visible. Only the later dispatcher denies calls.\"\nno B02.1 infra/terraform/iam.tf:47 'Resource = \"arn:aws:dynamodb:${var.region}:${data.aws_caller_identity.current.account_id}:table/clinic-agent-*\"' \"Runtime role gets PutItem/UpdateItem on every table matching clinic-agent-*, including the approvals and control tables, and GetSecretValue on clinic-agent/* for all clinics. Wildcard resources exceed the named tables the agent needs. H005 in github.tf is the deploy role, not this identity.\"\nno B02.2 src/tools/executor.ts:63 'const clinicId = typeof input.clinicId === \"string\" && input.clinicId ? input.clinicId : ctx.tenantId;' \"The tenant used for EHR credentials, payments and SMS secrets comes from a clinicId argument the model fills; it is not checked against ctx.tenantId or any claim. webchat.ts:43 also lets the x-clinic-id request header override the JWT clinic_id. The runtime role reads every clinic's secrets.\"\nno B02.3 src/integrations/ehr-mcp.ts:41 'body: new URLSearchParams({ grant_type: \"client_credentials\", client_id, client_secret, scope }),' \"The EHR token request sets no audience or resource, only scope. (Eligibility exchange and chat JWT checks do set audience.) Also payments and SMS use bearer keys with no audience.\"\nunk B03.1 \"Runtime credentials come from Secrets Manager and IRSA (ehr-mcp.ts:36, iam.tf:3), but the EHR client_secret, payments restricted_key and SMS api_token are static secrets. Whether those providers offer federated or short-lived alternatives is not stated in this repo.\"\nno B03.2 infra/terraform/main.tf:166 'resource \"aws_secretsmanager_secret\" \"payments\" {' \"IRSA and projected tokens have bounded lifetimes (iam.tf:5, deployment.yaml:111), but the EHR, payments, SMS and signing secrets have no aws_secretsmanager_secret_rotation or rotation setting anywhere in the repo.\"\nno B03.4 src/integrations/ehr-mcp.ts:58 'headers: { authorization: `Bearer ${token}`, \"x-clinic-id\": clinicId },' \"README says EHR uses mTLS, but the code only pins the server certificate (ehr-mcp.ts:20) and presents no client cert; the token is a plain bearer. Payments, SMS and eligibility calls also use plain bearer tokens with no DPoP or cert binding.\"\nunk B04.1 \"The agent has its own identity (iam.tf:1 role, per-clinic OAuth clients) so revoking it would not disable a user, but the repo has no script, runbook or deny list that revokes those credentials. The only control, the halted flag, does not revoke credentials. Revocation would live in IAM or the EHR IdP outside this repo.\"\nno B04.2 src/control/kill-switch.ts:48 'async assertRunning(tenantId: string): Promise<void> {' \"The only operator cutoff in the repo is the halted flag, read and enforced inside the agent process (assertRunning, watcher). It relies on the agent code cooperating. No gateway, IdP or target-service enforcement point is shown.\"\nno B04.3 src/integrations/ehr-mcp.ts:34 'if (hit && hit.exp - 30_000 > Date.now()) return hit.value;' \"EHR access tokens are cached until near expiry and sessions are cached for 4 minutes (ehr-mcp.ts:66); IRSA and workload tokens last up to 3600s/900s. No introspection, deny list or CAEP exists and no revocation time limit is stated anywhere.\"\nno B04.4 src/control/kill-switch.ts:70 'a.abort.abort(new Halted(' \"Halting only aborts in-flight client requests inside this process. No code revokes issued access tokens, EHR sessions, IRSA sessions or stored secrets, so they stay valid until expiry.\"\nno B05.1 config/policy.yaml:5 'highImpactTools:' \"The list covers only ehr__cancel_appointment, payments__refund_deposit and sms__send_freeform. Missing: ehr__update_appointment (can set status cancelled), insurance__check_eligibility (refunds deposits), sms__send_to_patient (outbound send). Unlisted tools default to allow once allowlisted (executor.ts:67).\"\nno B05.2 src/tools/approvals.ts:75 'if (rec.tool !== req.tool) return { ok: false, reason: \"approval is for a different tool\" };' \"checkApproval verifies tool, tenant, expiry and approver role but never compares rec.argsHash with the call's args; hashArgs is computed at request time (approvals.ts:49) and never checked. An approval for one deposit or patient message can authorize different arguments. The tenant compared is the model-chosen clinicId.\"\nno B05.3 src/workflows/eligibility-check.ts:40 'const refund = await payments.refundDeposit(' \"insurance__check_eligibility (not high-impact) calls payments.refundDeposit directly when the peer reports depositWaived, with no approval gate. Also ehr__update_appointment can set status cancelled (allowlist.yaml:16) without the cancel_appointment approval gate.\"\nno B05.4 infra/terraform/iam.tf:47 'Resource = \"arn:aws:dynamodb:${var.region}:${data.aws_caller_identity.current.account_id}:table/clinic-agent-*\"' \"Approvals live in clinic-agent-approvals, which the staff console should write (main.tf:95), but the agent runtime role has PutItem/UpdateItem on it (iam.tf:40-46), so the agent identity can create or alter approved records. Code does not do so; approver is otherwise a human role.\"\nno B05.5 src/tools/executor.ts:67 'if (policy.highImpactTools.includes(call.name)) {' \"The agent reads untrusted patient text and tool output, reaches PHI in the EHR, and acts outside (SMS, refunds, bookings). Only three tools are gated; ehr__book_appointment, ehr__update_appointment, sms__send_to_patient (vars) and the eligibility refund run ungated with model-chosen arguments. No plan-then-execute or capability tracking exists in code.\"\nans check B03.3 --met yes --evidence Dockerfile:12 --quote 'ENV NODE_ENV=production \\' --counter \"Grepped sk-, AKIA, password, api_key, secret across Dockerfile, config, prompts, release, k8s, terraform, workflows; only ARNs and secret resource names match, no secret values.\" --note \"No long-lived secret literals in prompts, image, or checked-in config.\"\n$PY scripts/review_coverage.py ledger $F B03.3 --rows ../agent/brace-coverage-B03.3.json --deviations ../agent/brace-empty.json --attempts ../agent/brace-empty.json"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2315,"cache_read_input_tokens":100365,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2315},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e9f926fe-86a1-4231-8f7e-512428ea3953","uuid":"d335faac-e2f9-4c0e-9afa-b7059aeb9154","timestamp":"2026-10-02T17:59:31.152Z","request_id":"req_011CfdqyWmooHy69qeDohPuo","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01QefHxVAZBsjfxZ3Yb6JsJD":{"command":"cd /private/var/folders/6v/yk9bzvrn5zx0kxll7d4szzb80000gn/T/brace-batch-48wveusy/skill; PY=/Users/brenn/.cache/uv/builds-v0/.tmpWHFCeM/bin/python; F=../agent/brace-findings.json\ncat > ../agent/brace-coverage-B03.3.json <<'E'\n[\n  {\"subject\": \"Dockerfile ENV and COPY\", \"status\": \"enforced\", \"evidence\": \"Dockerfile:12\", \"quote\": \"ENV NODE_ENV=production \\\\\", \"note\": \"Image sets only non-secret env and copies no .env file.\"},\n  {\"subject\": \"k8s ConfigMap secret reference\", \"status\": \"enforced\", \"evidence\": \"k8s/deployment.yaml:42\", \"quote\": \"SMS_SIGNING_SECRET_ARN: arn:aws:secretsmanager:us-west-2:418295730611:secret:clinic-agent/sms-signing\", \"note\": \"ConfigMap holds only a secret ARN, not a secret value.\"},\n  {\"subj