{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_017gkd4aTEc7fsPmwXgddXri","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /private/var/folders/6v/yk9bzvrn5zx0kxll7d4szzb80000gn/T/brace-batch-48wveusy/agent/brace-findings.json has been updated successfully."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e9f926fe-86a1-4231-8f7e-512428ea3953","uuid":"6eadca6e-504b-4cfd-8eab-f6384df8e29d","timestamp":"2026-10-02T17:59:56.064Z","tool_use_result":{"filePath":"/private/var/folders/6v/yk9bzvrn5zx0kxll7d4szzb80000gn/T/brace-batch-48wveusy/agent/brace-findings.json","oldString":"  \"repo\": \"\",","newString":"  \"repo\": \"clinic-agent (agent/)\",","originalFile":"{\n  \"brace_checklist\": \"2026-10-01\",\n  \"repo\": \"\",\n  \"commit\": null,\n  \"reviewed_at\": \"2026-10-02T17:56:08Z\",\n  \"scope\": \"TODO: what was reviewed and what wasn't.\",\n  \"review_protocol\": \"coverage-first-v1\",\n  \"findings\": [\n    {\n      \"item\": \"B01\",\n      \"gate\": \"G1\",\n      \"title\": \"Minimal tool surface\",\n      \"requirement\": \"List every built-in tool, MCP server, API, program, and file permission this agent type can use. Give a task-based reason for each. Enforce a role-based allowlist, and check that an unlisted tool can't be called. Don't base allow or approval decisions on hints a server gives about its own tools, such as \\\"read-only.\\\" MCP treats those hints as untrusted unless you trust the server.\",\n      \"not_covered\": [\n        {\n          \"problem\": \"A tool call that skips the MCP gateway or reaches a tool server directly\",\n          \"owner\": \"E06\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"problem\": \"A token or credential with too much access\",\n          \"owner\": \"B02\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"problem\": \"Hidden instructions inside a tool's description or schema\",\n          \"owner\": \"E04\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"problem\": \"A tool's description or schema changing after it was approved\",\n          \"owner\": \"E03\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"problem\": \"Lookalike or duplicate tool names across servers\",\n          \"owner\": \"E05\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"rating\": \"gap\",\n      \"confidence\": \"medium\",\n      \"evidence\": [\n        {\n          \"file\": \"config/tools.allowlist.yaml\",\n          \"line\": 4,\n          \"note\": \"One fixed literal YAML list of 11 names for the single scheduling_agent role.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"checks\": [\n        {\n          \"id\": \"B01.1\",\n          \"check\": \"Each agent role has one explicit allowlist of tool names, with no wildcard grants such as `*`, `mcp__*`, `Bash(*)`, or `bypassPermissions`.\",\n          \"verify\": \"1) Find where each agent is built and tools are passed (`allowed_tools`, `tools=[`, `allowedTools`, `.mcp.json`, `settings.json`). 2) Check each role has one fixed list of names. 3) Answer no if any list holds `*`, `mcp__*`, `Bash(*)`, a pattern or regex, `bypassPermissions`, or is built from `list_tools()`, or if a second agent role or entry point has no list.\",\n          \"met\": \"yes\",\n          \"evidence\": \"config/tools.allowlist.yaml:4\",\n          \"quote\": \"role: scheduling_agent\",\n          \"counter_search\": \"Searched for wildcard, mcp__, Bash(, bypassPermissions, list_tools-derived lists and other model entry points; classifier has no tools and reminders has no model.\",\n          \"note\": \"One fixed literal YAML list of 11 names for the single scheduling_agent role.\",\n          \"coverage\": [\n            {\n              \"subject\": \"scheduling agent role (loop.ts model call)\",\n              \"status\": \"enforced\",\n              \"evidence\": \"config/tools.allowlist.yaml:4\",\n              \"quote\": \"role: scheduling_agent\",\n              \"note\": \"One role has one fixed literal list of eleven tool names, no wildcards.\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"subject\": \"executor allowlist set\",\n              \"status\": \"enforced\",\n              \"evidence\": \"src/tools/executor.ts:20\",\n              \"quote\": \"const ALLOWED = new Set(allowlist.tools.map((t) => t.tool));\",\n              \"note\": \"The dispatcher builds its set only from the static YAML list.\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"subject\": \"intent classifier model call\",\n              \"status\": \"not_applicable\",\n              \"evidence\": \"src/agent/classifier.ts:46\",\n              \"quote\": \"model: CLASSIFIER_MODEL,\",\n              \"note\": \"Classifier request passes no tools parameter, so it needs no tool allowlist.\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"subject\": \"reminders cron entry point\",\n              \"status\": \"not_applicable\",\n              \"evidence\": \"src/workers/reminders.ts:9\",\n              \"quote\": \"// Daily reminder job (Kubernetes CronJob). Templated reminders only; no model involved.\",\n              \"note\": \"Second entry point has no model and no model-visible tools to list.\"\n            }\n          ],\n          \"deviations\": [],\n          \"attempts\": []\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"B01.2\",\n          \"check\": \"Tools discovered from MCP servers are filtered against that allowlist before the model can see or call them.\",\n          \"verify\": \"1) Find MCP discovery (`list_tools`, `session.list_tools`, `tools/list`, MCP client setup). 2) Trace the result to where it is handed to the model. 3) Confirm a filter keeps only names on the allowlist. 4) Answer no if any discovered tool reaches the model unfiltered, the filter is a denylist or prefix match (`startswith`, `mcp__server__`), or a refresh or reconnect path skips it.\",\n          \"met\": \"no\",\n          \"evidence\": \"src/agent/loop.ts:50\",\n          \"quote\": \"const tools = registry.definitions();\",\n          \"counter_search\": \"\",\n          \"note\": \"Every tool the EHR MCP server lists and the scanner accepts is registered and handed to the model; nothing filters registry.definitions() against config/tools.allowlist.yaml, so unlisted server tools (for example get_patient_contact) are model-visible. Only the later dispatcher denies calls.\",\n          \"coverage\": [],\n          \"deviations\": [],\n          \"attempts\": []\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"B01.3\",\n          \"check\": \"The dispatcher rejects a call to any tool name not on the allowlist, instead of looking it up dynamically.\",\n          \"verify\": \"1) Find the dispatcher (search `tool_use`, `call_tool`, `dispatch`, `execute`, `getattr`, `registry[`). 2) Check it rejects names not on the allowlist with an error. 3) Answer no if it looks tools up with `getattr`, `globals()`, `eval`, or a registry holding more than the allowlist, falls back to calling the MCP server directly, or catches the unknown-tool error and continues.\",\n          \"met\": \"yes\",\n          \"evidence\": \"src/tools/executor.ts:55\",\n          \"quote\": \"if (!ALLOWED.has(call.name)) return deny(\\\"not_allowlisted\\\");\",\n          \"counter_search\": \"Searched getattr/globals/eval/dynamic lookup and direct MCP fallback in dispatch; only Map get after the allowlist check, misses are denied.\",\n          \"note\": \"Unlisted tool names are denied and audited before registry lookup.\",\n          \"coverage\": [\n            {\n              \"subject\": \"executor allowlist rejection\",\n              \"status\": \"enforced\",\n              \"evidence\": \"src/tools/executor.ts:55\",\n              \"quote\": \"if (!ALLOWED.has(call.name)) return deny(\\\"not_allowlisted\\\");\",\n              \"note\": \"Unlisted names are denied with an audited error before any lookup.\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"subject\": \"registry lookup after allowlist\",\n              \"status\": \"enforced\",\n              \"evidence\": \"src/tools/executor.ts:57\",\n              \"quote\": \"if (!tool) return deny(\\\"not_registered\\\");\",\n              \"note\": \"Lookup is an exact Map get and a miss is denied, not continued.\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"subject\": \"no direct MCP fallback or dynamic lookup\",\n              \"status\": \"enforced\",\n              \"evidence\": \"src/tools/registry.ts:80\",\n              \"quote\": \"return this.tools.get(key);\",\n              \"note\": \"Registry get uses a plain Map with no getattr, eval, or fallback.\"\n            }\n          ],\n          \"deviations\": [],\n          \"attempts\": []\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"B01.4\",\n          \"check\": \"Allow and approval decisions never read server-supplied hints or descriptions such as `readOnlyHint` or 'read-only'.\",\n          \"verify\": \"1) Search for `readOnlyHint`, `destructiveHint`, `annotations`, `description`, and approval or auto-approve code. 2) Check whether any allow, skip-approval, or permission branch reads these. 3) Answer no if any allow or approval decision depends on a server hint or tool description text, including a default that auto-approves tools marked read-only.\",\n          \"met\": \"yes\",\n          \"evidence\": \"src/tools/executor.ts:67\",\n          \"quote\": \"if (policy.highImpactTools.includes(call.name)) {\",\n          \"counter_search\": \"Grepped readOnlyHint, destructiveHint, annotations, description across src; only metadata-scan reads annotations to reject, registry forwards description to the model; no allow or approval branch reads them.\",\n          \"note\": \"Approval depends on a static tool-name list, not server hints.\",\n          \"coverage\": [\n            {\n              \"subject\": \"executor approval decision\",\n              \"status\": \"enforced\",\n              \"evidence\": \"src/tools/executor.ts:67\",\n              \"quote\": \"if (policy.highImpactTools.includes(call.name)) {\",\n              \"note\": \"Approval branch keys only on a static policy list by tool name.\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"subject\": \"registry description handling\",\n              \"status\": \"enforced\",\n              \"evidence\": \"src/tools/registry.ts:164\",\n              \"quote\": \"description: t.description ?? \\\"\\\",\",\n              \"note\": \"Server description is only forwarded to the model, never branched on.\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"subject\": \"metadata-scan annotations use\",\n              \"status\": \"enforced\",\n              \"evidence\": \"src/tools/metadata-scan.ts:126\",\n              \"quote\": \"walkSchema(\\\"annotations\\\", t.annotations ?? {}, otherServerTools, f);\",\n              \"note\": \"Annotations are scanned for injection text and can only reject a tool.\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"subject\": \"allowlist config statement\",\n              \"status\": \"enforced\",\n              \"evidence\": \"config/tools.allowlist.yaml:3\",\n              \"quote\": \"# are not used for allow or approval decisions.\",\n              \"note\": \"Comment only; code inspection above confirms no hint-based branch.\"\n            }\n          ],\n          \"deviations\": [],\n          \"attempts\": []\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"B01.5\",\n          \"check\": \"File access is limited to named directories, not the whole filesystem.\",\n          \"verify\": \"1) Find file tools and mounts (`allowed_directories`, `cwd`, `open(`, `fs.`, `os.ReadFile`, container `volumes`, `mountPath`). 2) Check paths are resolved (`realpath`, `resolve`, `filepath.Clean`) then compared to named directories. 3) Answer no if access is unrestricted, `/` or home is mounted, the check is a string `startsWith`/prefix test without resolving `..` and symlinks, or a shell tool bypasses it.\",\n          \"met\": \"yes\",\n          \"evidence\": \"src/config.ts:41\",\n          \"quote\": \"return parse(readFileSync(join(ROOT, rel), \\\"utf8\\\")) as T;\",\n          \"counter_search\": \"Grepped fs, readFileSync, spawn, exec, eval in src; all reads use fixed paths; no file or shell tool is allowlisted; rootfs is read-only with only tmp and token mounts.\",\n          \"note\": \"No model-reachable file access; only fixed config and token paths are read.\",\n          \"coverage\": [\n            {\n              \"subject\": \"model-callable tools\",\n              \"status\": \"enforced\",\n              \"evidence\": \"config/tools.allowlist.yaml:26\",\n              \"quote\": \"- tool: insurance__check_eligibility\",\n              \"note\": \"No allowlisted tool reads or writes files, and no shell tool exists.\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"subject\": \"config and prompt readFileSync sites\",\n              \"status\": \"enforced\",\n              \"evidence\": \"src/config.ts:41\",\n              \"quote\": \"return parse(readFileSync(join(ROOT, rel), \\\"utf8\\\")) as T;\",\n              \"note\": \"Reads only fixed repo-relative config paths, never model-supplied paths.\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"subject\": \"workload token file read\",\n              \"status\": \"enforced\",\n              \"evidence\": \"src/agent/identity.ts:112\",\n              \"quote\": \"workloadToken: async () => readFileSync(WORKLOAD_TOKEN_PATH, \\\"utf8\\\").trim(),\",\n              \"note\": \"Reads one fixed token path set by environment, not by the model.\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"subject\": \"container mounts\",\n              \"status\": \"enforced\",\n              \"evidence\": \"k8s/deployment.yaml:101\",\n              \"quote\": \"- { name: tmp, mountPath: /tmp }\",\n              \"note\": \"Only a small memory tmp volume and a read-only token mount exist.\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"subject\": \"container root filesystem\",\n              \"status\": \"enforced\",\n              \"evidence\": \"k8s/deployment.yaml:89\",\n              \"quote\": \"readOnlyRootFilesystem: true\",\n              \"note\": \"Root filesystem is read-only so no wider writable area exists.\"\n            }\n          ],\n          \"deviations\": [],\n          \"attempts\": []\n        }\n      ],\n      \"red_flags_found\": [\n        \"src/agent/loop.ts:50 registry.definitions() hands all registered tools, not just allowlisted ones, to the model\"\n      ],\n      \"violates\": [\n        \"Enforce a role-based allowlist\"\n      ],\n      \"also_affects\": [],\n      \"summary\": \"The dispatcher denies unlisted tools, but every scanned EHR server tool is shown to the model without an allowlist filter.\",\n      \"next_step\": \"Filter registry.definitions() and MCP registration against config/tools.allowlist.yaml before the model sees any tool.\",\n      \"lead_role\": \"agent_team\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"item\": \"B02\",\n      \"gate\": \"G1\",\n      \"title\": \"Least-privilege access\",\n      \"requirement\": \"Limit credentials to named operations and resources, including tenant boundaries. Test that an allowed read works. Test that an out-of-scope write, an admin action, and a request for another tenant's data all fail. Limit each token to its intended audience, so other services reject it. Remove wildcard permissions and permissions inherited from people.\",\n      \"not_covered\": [\n        {\n          \"problem\": \"A retrieval search or cache not filtered by the requesting tenant or user\",\n          \"owner\": \"R04\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"problem\": \"Long-lived or static secrets that never expire or rotate\",\n          \"owner\": \"B03\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"problem\": \"Revocation delay from cached or self-contained tokens\",\n          \"owner\": \"B04\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"problem\": \"A sub-agent getting powers beyond its task, or a parent escalating through a peer\",\n          \"owner\": \"E08\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"problem\": \"Memory readable across tenants or tasks\",\n          \"owner\": \"R05\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"rating\": \"gap\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\",\n      \"evidence\": [\n        {\n          \"file\": \"infra/terraform/iam.tf\",\n          \"line\": 47,\n          \"note\": \"Runtime role gets PutItem/UpdateItem on every table matching clinic-agent-*, including the approvals and control tables, and GetSecretValue on clinic-agent/* for all clinics. Wildcard resources exceed the named tables the agent needs. H005 in github.tf is the deploy role, not this identity.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"checks\": [\n        {\n          \"id\": \"B02.1\",\n          \"check\": \"The agent's IAM policy or role names specific actions and resources, with no `*` action or resource and no owner, editor, or cluster-admin role.\",\n          \"verify\": \"1) Find IAM and RBAC files (`*.tf`, `iam*.json`, `Role`, `ClusterRoleBinding`, `RoleBinding`, CloudFormation). 2) Find the policy attached to the agent's identity. 3) Answer no if any `Action` or `Resource` is `*` or a service wildcard (`s3:*`), or it binds `roles/owner`, `roles/editor`, `cluster-admin`, or AdministratorAccess. Answer unknown if the agent's IAM is not in this repo.\",\n          \"met\": \"no\",\n          \"evidence\": \"infra/terraform/iam.tf:47\",\n          \"quote\": \"Resource = \\\"arn:aws:dynamodb:${var.region}:${data.aws_caller_identity.current.account_id}:table/clinic-agent-*\\\"\",\n          \"counter_search\": \"\",\n          \"note\": \"Runtime role gets PutItem/UpdateItem on every table matching clinic-agent-*, including the approvals and control tables, and GetSecretValue on clinic-agent/* for all clinics. Wildcard resources exceed the named tables the agent needs. H005 in github.tf is the deploy role, not this identity.\",\n          \"coverage\": [],\n          \"deviations\": [],\n          \"attempts\": []\n        },\n        {\n          \"