s not do so; approver is otherwise a human role.\",\n          \"coverage\": [],\n          \"deviations\": [],\n          \"attempts\": []\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"B05.5\",\n          \"check\": \"For an agent that reads untrusted input, reaches sensitive data or systems, and acts outside, every consequential action is gated, unless code shows untrusted content cannot pick the tool, destination, or arguments (for example plan-then-execute or capability tracking).\",\n          \"verify\": \"1) Check whether the agent reads untrusted content (web, email, files, tool output), reaches sensitive data, and can act outside. 2) If all three, list consequential actions and check each is gated. 3) Answer no if any is ungated and untrusted content can choose its tool, destination, or arguments with no plan-then-execute or capability tracking in code. Answer yes if the three are not combined.\",\n          \"met\": \"no\",\n          \"evidence\": \"src/tools/executor.ts:67\",\n          \"quote\": \"if (policy.highImpactTools.includes(call.name)) {\",\n          \"counter_search\": \"\",\n          \"note\": \"The agent reads untrusted patient text and tool output, reaches PHI in the EHR, and acts outside (SMS, refunds, bookings). Only three tools are gated; ehr__book_appointment, ehr__update_appointment, sms__send_to_patient (vars) and the eligibility refund run ungated with model-chosen arguments. No plan-then-execute or capability tracking exists in code.\",\n          \"coverage\": [],\n          \"deviations\": [],\n          \"attempts\": []\n        }\n      ],\n      \"red_flags_found\": [],\n      \"violates\": [\n        \"authorize its operation, target, and arguments\",\n        \"Test other tools and raw API or shell paths that could do the same thing\",\n        \"Block them by default in the execution path\"\n      ],\n      \"also_affects\": [\n        \"B02\"\n      ],\n      \"summary\": \"Approvals are not bound to arguments, and refund 