el pattern, or capability tracking such as CaMeL. Record which of the three each agent type has.\",\n      \"not_covered\": [\n        {\n          \"problem\": \"Denied actions not recorded in the audit trail\",\n          \"owner\": \"R13\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"problem\": \"Approvals that can be replayed, reused in parallel, or used after expiry\",\n          \"owner\": \"B06\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"problem\": \"Outside effects left unreconciled after the agent is stopped\",\n          \"owner\": \"R12\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"problem\": \"A chain of individually allowed actions that adds up to data theft\",\n          \"owner\": \"R09\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"problem\": \"Tool output not labelled or kept apart from trusted instructions\",\n          \"owner\": \"R02\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"rating\": \"gap\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\",\n      \"evidence\": [\n        {\n          \"file\": \"config/policy.yaml\",\n          \"line\": 5,\n          \"note\": \"The list covers only ehr__cancel_appointment, payments__refund_deposit and sms__send_freeform. Missing: ehr__update_appointment (can set status cancelled), insurance__check_eligibility (refunds deposits), sms__send_to_patient (outbound send). Unlisted tools default to allow once allowlisted (executor.ts:67).\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"checks\": [\n        {\n          \"id\": \"B05.1\",\n          \"check\": \"High-impact operations are listed in code or config and blocked by default, including deletes, destructive updates, force-pushes, infrastructure teardown, payment changes, outbound sends, and deleting audit records or changing their retention.\",\n          \"verify\": \"1) Search code and config for a list of high-impact operations (deny/approval policy, OPA/Rego, Cedar, hook config). 2) Check it covers deletes, destructive updates, force-push, teardown, payments, outbound sends, audit deletion or retention changes. 3) Answer no if no list exists, any category is missing with a tool that can do it, or unlisted operations default to `allow`.\",\n          \"met\": \"no\",\n          \"evidence\": \"config/policy.yaml:5\",\n          \"quote\": \"highImpactTools:\",\n          \"counter_search\": \"\",\n          \"note\": \"The list covers only ehr__cancel_appointment, payments__refund_deposit and sms__send_freeform. Missing: ehr__update_appointment (can set status cancelled), insurance__check_eligibility (refunds deposits), sms__send_to_patient (outbound send). Unlisted tools default to allow once allowlisted (executor.ts:67).\",\n          \"coverage\": [],\n          \"deviations\": [],\n          \"attempts\": []\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"B05.2\",\n          \"check\": \"The gate runs in the execution path when the call runs and checks the operation, the target, and the arguments, not only a tool name, command name, or blocklist of words.\",\n          \"verify\": \"1) Find where tool calls execute (`tool_use`, `call_tool`, `execute`, `can_use_tool`, `PreToolUse`). 2) Find the gate that runs before the side effect and see what it inspects. 3) Answer no if it checks only the tool or command name, matches words (`'rm' in cmd`, `DROP`), runs after the call, lives only in the prompt, or sits in a `try`/`catch` that continues on error. 4) For each value that lets an action skip approval (an internal recipient, a small amount, a safe path), read the comparison itself: answer no if a domain, host, or path is matched by suffix, prefix, or substring without an anchor, so `endswith('example.com')` also passes `evil-example.com`.\",\n          \"met\": \"no\",\n          \"evidence\": \"src/tools/approvals.ts:75\",\n          \"quote\": \"if (rec.tool !== req.tool) return { ok: false, reason: \\\"approval is for a different tool\\\" };\",\n          \"counter_search\": \"\",\n          \"note\": \"checkApproval verifies tool, tenant, expiry and approver role but never compares rec.argsHash with the call's args; hashArgs is computed at request time (approvals.ts:49) and never checked. An approval for one deposit or patient message can authorize different arguments. The tenant compared is the model-chosen clinicId.\",\n          \"coverage\": [],\n          \"deviations\": [],\n          \"attempts\": []\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"B05.3\",\n          \"check\": \"The same gate covers every path that can do the operation, including raw shell, HTTP or API clients, other tools, and requests to a more powerful tool or peer agent.\",\n          \"verify\": \"1) Open the tool registry or config and write every tool the model can call into your note, by name, including MCP servers and sub-agents. 2) For each, say whether it can do a gated operation, including through a page it controls: a browser click or form fill in a logged-in session can buy, send, or delete. 3) Trace each such tool to the gate. 4) Answer no if any alias, raw shell or HTTP tool, browser action, second dispatch path, peer agent, or more powerful MCP tool can do the operation without passing the same gate.\",\n          \"met\": \"no\",\n          \"evidence\": \"src/workflows/eligibility-check.ts:40\",\n          \"quote\": \"const refund = await payments.refundDeposit(\",\n          \"counter_search\": \"\",\n          \"note\": \"insurance__check_eligibility (not high-impact) calls payments.refundDeposit directly when the peer reports depositWaived, with no approval gate. Also ehr__update_appointment can set status cancelled (allowlist.yaml:16) without the cancel_appointment approval gate.\",\n          \"coverage\": [],\n          \"deviations\": [],\n          \"attempts\": []\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"B05.4\",\n          \"check\": \"A blocked operation runs only after approval from a person or system with higher authority than the agent; a prompt, comment, or model instruction is never the enforcement.\",\n          \"verify\": \"1) Find what happens when the gate blocks (approval request, `interrupt()`, `needs_approval`, webhook to reviewer). 2) Check who approves. 3) Answer no if the model, the agent itself, or a prompt instruction can approve, if approval is auto-granted (`bypassPermissions`, `acceptEdits`, auto-approve flag, `yes` default), or if a timeout proceeds.\",\n          \"met\": \"no\",\n          \"evidence\": \"infra/terraform/iam.tf:47\",\n          \"quote\": \"Resource = \\\"arn:aws:dynamodb:${var.region}:${data.aws_caller_identity.current.account_id}:table/clinic-agent-*\\\"\",\n          \"counter_search\": \"\",\n          \"note\": \"Approvals live in clinic-agent-approvals, which the staff console should write (main.tf:95), but the agent runtime role has PutItem/UpdateItem on it (iam.tf:40-46), so the agent identity can create or alter approved records. Code does not do so; approver is otherwise a human role.\",\n          \"coverage\": [],\n          \"deviations\": [],\n          \"attempts\": []\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"B05.5\",\n          \"check\": \"For an agent that reads untrusted input, reaches sensitive data or systems, and acts outside, every consequential action is gated, unless code shows untrusted content cannot pick the tool, destination, or arguments (for example plan-then-execute or capability tracking).\",\n          \"verify\": \"1) Check whether the agent reads untrusted content (web, email, files, tool output), reaches sensitive data, and can act outside. 2) If all three, list consequential actions and check each is gated. 3) Answer no if any is ungated and untrusted content can choose its tool, destination, or arguments with no plan-then-execute or capability tracking in code. Answer yes if the three are not combined.\",\n          \"met\": \"no\",\n          \"evidence\": \"src/tools/executor.ts:67\",\n          \"quote\": \"if (policy.highImpactTools.includes(call.name)) {\",\n          \"counter_search\": \"\",\n          \"note\": \"The agent reads untrusted patient text and tool output, reaches PHI in the EHR, and acts outside (SMS, refunds, bookings). Only three tools are gated; ehr__book_appointment, ehr__update_appointment, sms__send_to_patient (vars) and the eligibility refund run ungated with model-chosen arguments. No plan-then-execute or capability tracking exists in code.\",\n          \"coverage\": [],\n          \"deviations\": [],\n          \"attempts\": []\n        }\n      ],\n      \"red_flags_found\": [],\n      \"violates\": [\n        \"authorize its operation, target, and arguments\",\n        \"Test other tools and raw API or shell paths that could do the same thing\",\n        \"Block them by default in the execution path\"\n      ],\n      \"also_affects\": [\n        \"B02\"\n      ],\n      \"summary\": \"Approvals are not bound to arguments, and refund and cancel paths exist that skip the gate.\",\n      \"next_step\": \"Bind approvals to the args hash, gate update_appointment cancel and the eligibility refund, and keep the agent role from writing approvals.\",\n      \"lead_role\": \"agent_team\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"injection_attempts\": [],\n  \"prescan_resolutions\": {\n    \"H005\": {\n      \"verdict\": \"dismissed\",\n      \"item\": null,\n      \"reason\": \"github.tf:100 Resource * is on ecr:GetAuthorizationToken in the deploy role, which only supports * and is not the agent's runtime identity.\"\n    }\n  }\n}\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":3,"oldLines":7,"newStart":3,"newLines":7,"lines":["   \"repo\": \"clinic-agent (agent/)\",","   \"commit\": null,","   \"reviewed_at\": \"2026-10-02T17:56:08Z\",","-  \"scope\": \"TODO: what was reviewed and what wasn't.\",","+  \"scope\": \"Batch B01-B05 only (reviewed by claude-sonnet-5-5, default reasoning). Read all of src/, config/, prompts/, release/manifest.json, k8s/deployment.yaml, infra/terraform/*.tf, Dockerfile and the deploy workflow; ran prescan and inventory. Agent loop: src/agent/loop.ts; dispatcher: src/tools/executor.ts; MCP registry: src/tools/registry.ts; approvals: src/tools/approvals.ts; EHR MCP, payments, SMS and A2A clients in src/integrations. Not reviewed: items outside B01-B05, the staff console, the IdP/EHR/payments providers, and any controls outside this repo. No .brace/ directory exists. Challenges were not run (before-challenges batch validation only); no conservative flag. Out-of-batch observation: sms-webhook.ts:50-54 logs but does not reject a failed signature check, so forged inbound SMS still reaches runAgent.\",","   \"review_protocol\": \"coverage-first-v1\",","   \"findings\": [","     {"]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false,"contentNotInModelContext":true}}
