{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfdr3uEmvjFhr1FBmSot7","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I reviewed B01–B05 and saved the findings in `agent/brace-findings.json`. All five items are rated `gap`. The batch validator (`--batch B01,B02,B03,B04,B05 --before-challenges --fix`) printed `Valid. gap: 5. Injection attempts: 0.` I did not run challenges, and I used normal mode.\n\n**B01 (minimal tool surface), medium confidence**\n- B01.1, B01.3, B01.4 and B01.5 are `yes`.\n- B01.2 is `no`. `registry.definitions()` hands every scanned EHR tool to the model (`src/agent/loop.ts:50`), with no filter against the allowlist. The dispatcher still denies unlisted calls.\n\n**B02 (least-privilege access), high confidence**\n- The model chooses the clinic. `clinicId` comes from the tool input (`src/tools/executor.ts:63`), and the webchat `x-clinic-id` header overrides the JWT's clinic claim (`src/routes/webchat.ts:43`).\n- The runtime role has write access to every `clinic-agent-*` DynamoDB table (`infra/terraform/iam.tf:47`).\n- The EHR token request sets no audience (`src/integrations/ehr-mcp.ts:41`).\n- B02.4 is `yes`.\n\n**B03 (credential lifetime and handling), medium confidence**\n- B03.2 is `no`: the EHR, payments, SMS and signing secrets have no rotation configured (`infra/terraform/main.tf:166`).\n- B03.4 is `no`: the EHR client presents a plain bearer token (`src/integrations/ehr-mcp.ts:58`), although the README says it uses mTLS.\n- B03.1 is `unknown`, because I can't tell from the repo whether the providers offer short-lived alternatives.\n- B03.3 is `yes`.\n\n**B04 (independent revocation), high confidence**\n- The only cutoff is the halt flag, which is checked inside the agent (B04.2, B04.4). Tokens and sessions are cached with no stated revocation time limit (B04.3).\n- B04.1 is `unknown`, because any revoke path would live outside this repo.\n\n**B05 (destructive-action interception), high confidence**\n- The high-impact list is incomplete (B05.1).\n- `checkApproval` never compares the stored `argsHash` with the call's arguments (`src/tools/approvals.ts:75`).\n- `insurance__check_eligibility` refunds deposits with no approval (`src/workflows/eligibility-check.ts:40`), and `ehr__update_appointment` can set a status of cancelled without the cancel gate.\n- The agent's IAM role can write the approvals table (B05.4).\n- Several consequential tools run ungated while untrusted patient text picks their arguments (B05.5).\n- `iam.tf:47` fails both B02 and B05.4, so each item lists the other under `also_affects`.\n\n**Prescan:** H005 (`infra/terraform/github.tf:100`, `Resource = \"*\"`) is dismissed. It sits on the deploy role's `ecr:GetAuthorizationToken` statement, not the agent's identity. I left the other prescan hits (B11, R13, E03) alone because they belong to other batches.\n\n**Injection attempts:** none found.\n\n**Out-of-batch observation (recorded in `scope`):** a failed inbound SMS signature check is logged but not rejected (`src/routes/sms-webhook.ts:50-54`), so a forged SMS still reaches the agent.\n\n**Extra files:** I added scratch files to the workspace: `brace-coverage-*.json`, `brace-empty.json`, `brace-inventory.json` and `brace-prescan.json`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1324,"cache_read_input_tokens":111234,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1324},"output_tokens":839,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e9f926fe-86a1-4231-8f7e-512428ea3953","uuid":"8f2557fc-d1b0-400b-8c95-a1553edb211b","timestamp":"2026-10-02T18:00:10.900Z","request_id":"req_011Cfdr3tvvE53Wqymuh2GiX"}
